        <body>
            <div xml:id="d861">

                <pb facs="1052" n="942" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg942"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./77: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-17T13:00:00+08:00">March 17, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 17—3:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 17, noon. I have received today the following telegram from Dr.
                            Skinsnes concerning Nelson and Tvedt: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘Letter from prisoners dated March 11th states health good, not
                                    further tortured, located Kenchiatawu 37 li east of
                                    Chiliping.’</p>
                            </quote></p>
                        <p>Above information as regards location of captives has been communicated
                            to Chinese authorities.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Nanking and Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
